WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.223
The Audit Trail module keeps a log of changes and events in the back end.

00:00:05.223 --> 00:00:09.500
Its settings decide which events are recorded, how long they are kept, and

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.264
what is stored about users.

00:00:11.264 --> 00:00:13.670
In this video, you set up each of them.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:22.492
Audit Trail and Users Audit Trail are two separate features.

00:00:22.492 --> 00:00:28.760
Enable both under Tools, Features, and their settings pages become available under Settings.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:33.657
Settings, Audit Trail has an Events tab and a Trimming tab, and a

00:00:33.657 --> 00:00:36.869
Content tab when the Contents feature is enabled.

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:42.300
Settings, Security, User Audit Trail is a separate page for what is stored about users.

00:00:46.517 --> 00:00:48.854
Let's open Settings, Audit Trail.

00:00:48.854 --> 00:00:53.770
The Events tab lists every event the module can record, grouped by category,

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:57.007
each with a description and an Enabled checkbox.

00:00:57.478 --> 00:01:00.744
The Content category covers content items:

00:01:00.744 --> 00:01:05.914
created, saved, published, unpublished, removed, cloned, and restored.

00:01:05.914 --> 00:01:10.608
The User category covers sign-ins and changes to user accounts.

00:01:11.078 --> 00:01:13.701
Each category has a Select all checkbox.

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:18.206
Login failed is the one built-in event that starts switched off, so let's

00:01:18.206 --> 00:01:21.058
select it to record failed sign-in attempts.

00:01:21.518 --> 00:01:26.697
Below the table, Allow client IP address adds the address each event came from.

00:01:26.697 --> 00:01:31.268
An IP address can be personal data, so check the rules for your site.

00:01:31.268 --> 00:01:32.608
Let's select it.

00:01:33.063 --> 00:01:35.574
Content events need one more choice.

00:01:35.574 --> 00:01:40.537
On the Content tab, Allowed content types starts with nothing selected, so no

00:01:40.537 --> 00:01:44.363
content events are recorded until you select at least one.

00:01:44.856 --> 00:01:46.250
Let's select Page.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:50.198
An event is recorded only when it is enabled on the Events tab

00:01:50.198 --> 00:01:53.856
and, for content, when its content type is selected here.

00:01:54.316 --> 00:01:55.452
Select Save.

00:01:55.452 --> 00:02:00.056
The message Site settings updated successfully confirms the change.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.878
Events add up, so the module trims them.

00:02:06.878 --> 00:02:08.820
Let's open the Trimming tab.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:13.560
Retention period is the number of days an event is kept, and it starts at 10.

00:02:14.019 --> 00:02:18.549
A background task deletes the events older than the retention period.

00:02:18.549 --> 00:02:23.019
By default, it runs once a day, and Last run shows when it last ran.

00:02:23.469 --> 00:02:26.332
Let's keep events for 90 days instead.

00:02:26.332 --> 00:02:28.609
Select the field and type 90.

00:02:29.071 --> 00:02:33.057
To keep events indefinitely, you would select Disable trimming task.

00:02:33.057 --> 00:02:35.481
Let's leave it cleared and select Save.

00:02:39.681 --> 00:02:43.771
For each property of a user, you choose how its value is stored.

00:02:43.771 --> 00:02:45.466
Store keeps it as text.

00:02:45.466 --> 00:02:51.251
PartialAsteriskRedactor keeps the first and last character and hides the rest with asterisks.

00:02:52.001 --> 00:02:58.759
ErasingRedactor stores an empty value, which shows that the property had a value without revealing it.

00:02:58.759 --> 00:03:03.891
HmacRedactor stores a hash, a scrambled form that cannot be turned back into

00:03:03.891 --> 00:03:07.771
the value, and is offered only when a key is configured.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:13.976
Settings, Security, User Audit Trail lists User Properties to Store.

00:03:13.976 --> 00:03:18.385
By default, a user event stores the user's name and ID, and these

00:03:18.385 --> 00:03:22.360
settings add a User Snapshot of the properties you choose.

00:03:22.811 --> 00:03:27.120
Each property of a user has its own drop-down, and every one starts

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.190
empty, which means the property is not stored.

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:34.381
The password hash, reset token and user tokens are never offered.

00:03:34.844 --> 00:03:37.973
Let's choose PartialAsteriskRedactor for Email.

00:03:37.973 --> 00:03:41.634
Then select Save, and the page reloads with your choice.

00:03:42.095 --> 00:03:47.351
With properties chosen, a snapshot is saved when a user is created, updated,

00:03:47.351 --> 00:03:49.786
enabled, disabled, or confirmed.

00:03:49.786 --> 00:03:54.145
It appears as User Snapshot on the Details page of that event.

00:03:54.607 --> 00:03:58.413
When a user is deleted, the snapshots of that user are removed from

00:03:58.413 --> 00:04:00.707
the earlier events of the Audit Trail.

00:04:04.932 --> 00:04:09.226
Under Tools, Audit Trail, the list shows what these settings produce.

00:04:09.226 --> 00:04:13.406
Someone tried to sign in with an unknown user name, and that failed

00:04:13.406 --> 00:04:17.242
attempt appears as a Login failed event in the User category.

00:04:17.744 --> 00:04:23.372
Entries recorded after you allowed the client IP address carry a badge with that address.

00:04:23.372 --> 00:04:27.874
A published Page appears too, because Page is an allowed content type.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:31.094
Select Details on the Login failed entry.

00:04:31.094 --> 00:04:35.724
Event Info lists the category, the event name, who triggered it and when,

00:04:35.724 --> 00:04:37.600
and the Client IP address.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:42.002
Three settings shape the Audit Trail:

00:04:42.002 --> 00:04:46.807
which events it records, how long it keeps them, and what it stores about users.

00:04:46.807 --> 00:04:48.260
Thanks for watching.

